{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Irreducible"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch.no_branch_section","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch.no_branch_section","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicNoBranch.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**No single-valued algebraic branch** of the color cubic (conditional on its computed\nirreducibility over the base field). If the cubic `C` is irreducible and has degree > 1,\nno element of the field is a root — i.e. there is no single-valued branch section. This is\nthe permanent consequence of the witness's `monodromy = S₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch.no_root_of_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCubicNoBranch.no_root_of_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCubicNoBranch.lean#L34-L55","doc":"**An irreducible polynomial of degree > 1 over a field has no root.** A root `a` gives\n`(X − C a) ∣ p`; since `X − C a` is not a unit and `p` is irreducible, `p` is associate to\n`X − C a`, forcing `natDegree p = 1` — contradicting `1 < natDegree p`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}